WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:09.140
Welcome to DBL Group's TalentHub!
Need new people for your unit?

2
00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:12.820
In this video we'll see how
to raise a requisition, where

3
00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:18.300
it goes once you submit it, and what to
do if it comes back to you. Let's begin!

4
00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:20.930
You don't need to ask for this role.

5
00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:26.290
When the Head of Talent Acquisition
names you as your unit's

6
00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:30.570
raiser in Approval Paths,
the access appears in your account.

7
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:34.240
To sign in, enter your official
DBL email and your password.

8
00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:39.440
On your own computer, tick Remember me
so your email is filled in next time.

9
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.120
Now click Sign in.

10
00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:46.990
The paper Employee Requisition
Form now lives in TalentHub.

11
00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:53.070
Your job is two things:
give the position details,

12
00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:56.540
and say which facilities the new
employee needs. Choosing approvers,

13
00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:59.580
approving your own requisition
or reviewing CVs are not part of it.

14
00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:03.980
The main menu is on the left:
Dashboard, Requisitions, Organogram,

15
00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:09.460
Employees and Notifications. Most of
your work happens under Requisitions.

16
00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:12.810
Now let's raise a new requisition.

17
00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:19.130
The form has just two steps:
the position details first,

18
00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:22.550
then the new employee's facilities.
Start by clicking Requisitions.

19
00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:28.200
The tiles at the top show how many of
your requisitions are at each stage,

20
00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.640
with the full list below.

21
00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:35.760
For a new one,
click New requisition on the right.

22
00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:41.430
Notice that Raising as already shows
your name, and Unit / Factory your unit.

23
00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:46.150
If you may raise for more than one unit,
choose it here.

24
00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:49.390
Then pick the Line of Business.

25
00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:53.700
Under Department,
choose the one that needs the person.

26
00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:59.222
We're taking Plant HR. If there's
a particular section, add that too.

27
00:01:59.690 --> 00:02:04.740
In Designation / Job title,
give the post, here Executive.

28
00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:10.290
Could someone at Officer
or Senior Officer level fit too?

29
00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:15.290
Then add those levels with
Add another designation.

30
00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:19.200
Requisition type says
why you need someone.

31
00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:24.240
A new position is New; filling the
place of someone who left is Replace.

32
00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:29.640
Ours is a replacement,
so we choose Replace.

33
00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:32.750
In Employee,
find the person being replaced,

34
00:02:32.870 --> 00:02:35.870
here Sadia Islam.

35
00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:41.870
Under Reason for leaving, give the reason,
such as Better Opportunity.

36
00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:46.870
Replacing more than one person?
Use Add another employee.

37
00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:52.380
In Nos. of required post,

38
00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:57.661
enter how many you need,
here one. Total no.

39
00:02:57.781 --> 00:03:01.540
of vacant post beside it fills
itself from the organogram.

40
00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:07.130
In Place of posting,
choose the workplace, here Jinnat Complex.

41
00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:11.210
Give the Vacant date,
when the post fell empty,

42
00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:15.490
and When needed,
the date you need someone by.

43
00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:20.280
Priority says how urgent it is;
we're setting Moderate.

44
00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:26.480
Then the type of post: Permanent,
Temporary or Contractual.

45
00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:28.960
Now click Next.

46
00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:32.310
This is step two, Facility Requirements.

47
00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:38.790
Choose only what is really needed.
For a laptop or desktop,

48
00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:45.310
tick Needed under Laptop / Desktop,
then pick the device, here Laptop.

49
00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:51.860
One important point. Choosing Transport
or Dormitory doesn't guarantee them.

50
00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:57.260
Transport depends on the route, the timing
and seats; a dormitory bed on vacancies

51
00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:02.860
and allocation. These conditions
are written right on the form.

52
00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:07.570
Last, Seating Arrangement.
If a seat is needed, tick Needed and say

53
00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:13.570
whether an existing seat is free or a
new one is needed, here Existing seat.

54
00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:19.450
Check everything once, then click Send for
job analysis. That's it, it's submitted!

55
00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:25.440
The requisition is created, and the
system has given it its own number.

56
00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:32.160
Its status is now Job Analysis,
which means it's with your

57
00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:36.600
unit's Factory HR team,
and they've already been notified.

58
00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:41.949
Remember this. After you submit,
the requisition doesn't go straight to

59
00:04:42.069 --> 00:04:47.470
the approvers. It goes to Factory
HR first. They fill in Section B,

60
00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:53.350
the job description, qualifications and
experience, and attach the detailed JD.

61
00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:58.859
Then the approvals begin.
The Approvals tab shows who will approve,

62
00:04:58.979 --> 00:05:02.700
who already has, when, and any comments.

63
00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:07.940
The requisition goes to each
approver in turn, in a set order.

64
00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:14.090
Good to know: a requisition’s approval
chain is saved the moment you raise it.

65
00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:18.690
Changing Approval Paths later never
changes the chain of one already raised.

66
00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:22.680
The statuses at a glance. Job Analysis:

67
00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:28.840
Factory HR is preparing the position.
Pending Approval: approvals under way.

68
00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:35.280
Approved: all approvals done.
Profile Ready: the role profile is ready.

69
00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:41.360
Posted: the ad is on the careers page.
Rejected: not approved.

70
00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:45.270
A requisition can come
back to you in two ways.

71
00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:50.230
First, when Factory HR
needs more information.

72
00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:55.150
You'll get a notification;
click the bell at the top to open it.

73
00:05:55.500 --> 00:06:00.820
In the Job Analysis tab,
Factory HR's note tells you what to fix.

74
00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:04.540
The status stays Job Analysis;

75
00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:08.940
the requisition is only
with you for the correction.

76
00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:14.930
Click Edit details and correct it,
here the Vacant date.

77
00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:19.610
Then click Save changes.

78
00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:23.201
Now click Resend for job analysis.

79
00:06:23.561 --> 00:06:26.680
The requisition goes back to Factory HR.

80
00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:33.070
The second case: during approval,
an approver chooses Need more info.

81
00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:38.710
Approval pauses
and the requisition comes back to you.

82
00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:43.110
Read their remark under Sent back to you
for clarification in the Approvals tab.

83
00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:49.420
Fix anything needed through Edit details,
then click Send for approval.

84
00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:53.020
Remember, the chain starts
again from the first level,

85
00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:55.140
and every approver looks at it afresh.

86
00:06:55.490 --> 00:07:01.050
If a requisition is Rejected, that's
the end of it, and the reason is in the

87
00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:07.090
Approvals tab. Still need someone?
Raise a new one. You can't withdraw a

88
00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:12.450
submitted requisition yourself; if it's
no longer needed, tell whoever has it now.

89
00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:16.560
When every approver has signed,
the status becomes Approved.

90
00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:20.920
Then the Head of Talent
Acquisition picks the CV sources

91
00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:26.600
and assigns a Corporate Recruiter,
who runs the hiring through to onboarding.

92
00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:29.760
You’ll be told at every step.

93
00:07:30.110 --> 00:07:34.577
A small tip: before raising a
requisition, check the posts

94
00:07:34.697 --> 00:07:39.390
and vacancies in the organogram.
You'll see exactly where your unit stands.

95
00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:46.101
When something happens, a number
appears on the bell, with a short sound

96
00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:52.260
and a message on screen. The page
updates by itself, no refreshing needed.

97
00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:57.500
To see them all, open Notifications;
the important ones also arrive by email.

98
00:07:57.850 --> 00:07:58.990
Don't want the emails?

99
00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:04.490
Turn off Email notifications under
the Notifications tab in Settings.

100
00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:09.120
A few common questions. Your unit
isn't in the Unit / Factory list,

101
00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:13.160
or you see Approval path not found?

102
00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:18.240
Then the raiser or the chain for your
unit isn't set up in Approval Paths yet.

103
00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:23.400
Contact Factory HR
or the Head of Talent Acquisition.

104
00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:27.071
As a raiser you can't see candidates' CVs.

105
00:08:27.831 --> 00:08:33.910
But if you're invited to an interview
panel, you'll find it under My Interviews.

106
00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:37.500
The full guide is a PDF under Tutorials.

107
00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:42.060
For access, ask Factory HR
or the Head of Talent Acquisition;

108
00:08:42.340 --> 00:08:47.700
for sign-in trouble, the IT Helpdesk.
Thank you for using TalentHub.

